Cosmos look: dark title bars, the Cosmos icon in the Dock, Cosmos in the bottle-update window.

- winemac: Mac Driver option Appearance. By default every Wine window, title
  bar and Mac dialog uses macOS's dark appearance (NSAppearanceNameDarkAqua),
  like Cosmopolitan. "light" forces light, "system" follows macOS. Read with
  the other options before the Cocoa app starts.
- winemac: every program shows the Cosmos icon in the Dock
  (share/wine/cosmos/exeIcon.icns, found next to winemac.so), the owner's
  choice. Mac Driver option ProgramIcon=y shows the program's own icon
  instead; a program without one still gets the Cosmos icon (CrossOver's hack
  13440 only looked for CrossOver.app's exeIcon.icns through CX_ROOT).
- winemac: the icon goes to the Dock at once (setApplicationIconImage). The
  applicationIcon property alone only reached the Dock on the next switch to
  the foreground. Found by Cursor.
- wineboot: the window shown while a bottle is created or updated says
  "Cosmos is getting the bottle in ... ready" under the title "Cosmos". Its
  icon is user32's IDI_WINLOGO, which the Cosmos build replaces with the
  Cosmos icon (cosmos-theme/oic_winlogo.ico).

